Explanation:

Differentiating both equations implicitly with respect to $z$ at $(1,1,1)$ yields:
$ 2 (d x / d z) + 3 (d y / d z) + 4 = 0 $
$ 2 (d x / d z) + 2 (d y / d z) + 2 = 0 $
Solving this linear system gives $d y / d z = -2$ and $d x / d z = 1$.
